# ort-server decision operator set (opt-in): default.required_operators.config plus the four entries the
# decision models need beyond it (ai.onnx 13 GatherElements, IsNaN, Max; ai.onnx 16 GreaterOrEqual):
#   - SupersonicLabs/Julia-1 (export SupersonicLabs/Julia-1-ONNX @82a2fad, decision head)
#   - convaiinnovations/laya (export onnx-community/laya-ONNX @42e2a6e, decision head)
# each converted with onnxruntime 1.31.1 convert_onnx_models_to_ort --optimization_style Runtime. Their graphs
# take decision-head inputs (marker_pos, marker_mask, qtype) that /classify does not build yet, so the default
# build leaves these out. 77 operator entries. Build: tools/ort-musl-build.sh <arch>
# ops/decision.required_operators.config <dir>
ai.onnx;1;GlobalAveragePool,Not
ai.onnx;6;HardSigmoid
ai.onnx;7;And,Cos,Sin
ai.onnx;9;ConstantOfShape,Where
ai.onnx;11;AveragePool,Conv,ConvTranspose,NonMaxSuppression,Range,TopK
ai.onnx;12;Einsum,LessOrEqual,MaxPool
ai.onnx;13;Abs,Cast,Clip,Concat,DequantizeLinear,Equal,Erf,Exp,Expand,Flatten,Gather,GatherElements,GatherND,Gemm,IsNaN,Less,Log,MatMul,Max,Min,Neg,NonZero,Pad,Pow,QuantizeLinear,ReduceL2,ReduceMax,ReduceMean,ReduceSum,Resize,ScatterND,Shape,Sigmoid,Slice,Softmax,Split,Sqrt,Squeeze,Tanh,Transpose,Unsqueeze
ai.onnx;14;Add,CumSum,Div,LSTM,Mul,Relu,Reshape,Sub
ai.onnx;15;Pow,Shape
ai.onnx;16;GreaterOrEqual,LessOrEqual,ScatterND,Where
ai.onnx;17;LayerNormalization
ai.onnx;18;Split
com.microsoft;1;FusedConv,QLinearConv,QLinearSigmoid
